*Title: INSTALLATION
*Author: Will

* VERSION

$Id: INSTALL,v 1.3 2002/02/06 23:10:24 willhelm Exp $

For more up-to-date documentation, check out the web-site at:
http://lyntin.sourceforge.net/



* SUMMARY

This file holds installation instructions for Lyntin.  It should be
revisited and re-written at some point.



* UNIX/LINUX

	1. make sure you have at least Python 2.0--You can do this by 
	   running "python" and seeing what version it says it is.  If 
	   you don't have Python 2.0 or later installed, Lyntin won't work.
	2. download the version of Lyntin you're looking for (below) 
	3. untar the client into ~/lyntin or something along those lines
	4. do "chmod 777 lyntin.py" to set the lyntin.py file to be executable
	5. run lyntin.py

lyntin.py takes a series of options.  For a list of options 
and explanations, run:

^<<
   lyntin.py --help
^>>



* WINDOWS

	1. make sure you have at least Python 2.0
	2. unzip the client into c:\lyntin
	3. double-click on lyntin.py to run lyntin
	4. probably want to build a shortcut for Lyntin to make it easier
	   to run from your desktop.  the shortcut should use pythonw.exe
	   instead of python.exe--this will start Lyntin without that silly
	   extra window.
